KG42.register("clusters-d1ee893ff975ba351cb5e041",{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v142-d-CL001","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","label":"Bilateral bid-driven PBUC limits, NIRA scheduling, and local pricing","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Bilateral bid-driven PBUC limits, NIRA scheduling, and local pricing","market_meaning":"Retailers submit all-day supply and demand bids to the MO; PBUC performs initial allocation according to shortage and unsold-surplus conditions respectively and forms trading upper limits, NIRA uses the relevant inputs to calculate participant schedules, and then the MO combines the scheduled quantities and bids to form the local MCP. The current chain can form a process candidate, but gaps remain in the limit identity, price roles, and mathematical closure.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination","matching","clearing","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The chains belong to the day-ahead local market of the same mechanism, but the supplier award and the demand-side surplus purchase must retain their trigger conditions separately. The correspondence between the PBUC award upper limit and the expected-value upper limit, the use of H-MG bids, and the general applicability of case parameters remain unresolved, and strict equivalence or complete optimization cannot be claimed on the basis of common nodes.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is determined based on the explicit information dependencies among bid inputs, initial-allocation limits, final scheduling, and pricing. The institutional form of the MO and the execution locations of Steps 1 and 2 are retained as organizational background; upstream forecasts and initial schedules are treated as external inputs, while transaction execution and payment are assembled separately. The PBUC content overlapping between R003 and R006 belongs to different expressions of the same initial-allocation process.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Gives the price-quantity block format of the retailer demand bid as an input to the initial allocation of surplus purchase and subsequent pricing."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Gives the retailer supply bid format and retains its use for H-MG shortage."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Supplements the responsibility for submitting all-day bids to the MO; the institutional form and the execution locations of the first two steps are optional organizational arrangements, and no algorithmic dependency is added on that basis."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Supplements, from the matching perspective, the PBUC supply-demand priority principle and the H-MG supplier scope; award content overlapping with R003 is not counted as an additional independent market rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the main trunk through which the PBUC initial-allocation limits enter NIRA scheduling, as well as the frozen balance, retailer boundary, and expected-value objects."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Connects the final scheduled quantities and supply-demand bids to the MO's MCP calculation, forming the price output of this process."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e003"],"rationale":"In the same mechanism, the demand bid block format and the responsibility for submitting all-day bids to the MO are complementary, answering respectively what is submitted and to whom it is submitted."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e003"],"rationale":"The block format of the supply bid and the responsibility for submitting all-day bids to the MO jointly define the supply-side declaration interface."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e013"],"rationale":"The retailer demand bid for purchasing H-MG surplus electricity is the price input for demand-side PBUC allocation; this relation applies only when unsold surplus electricity exists."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e012"],"rationale":"The retailer supply bid enters the supplier price ranking covering the total H-MG shortage; R006 additionally involves H-MG surplus suppliers, and the two types of supplier identities cannot therefore be equated."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"rationale":"The citation explicitly feeds both the supply and demand groups of PBUC upper bounds into Step 4. The functional interface between initial allocation and dispatch is assembled here, but it is not claimed that the award quantities of the initial allocation have already been brought into strict correspondence with the expected values in Eq. (20)–(22)."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e013"],"rationale":"Both items describe the same demand-side PBUC purchase award and upper-bound result. R006 additionally contains a priority-order expression, which is retained as an alternative expression pending verification, and an independent rule is not added on this basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R003::x::var_nira_x_i"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R009::E::v141-c-R009-E003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e032"],"rationale":"The participant dispatch output by Step 4 is the quantity input in the price-quantity pairs of Step 5. This is a quantity interface made explicit by the citation, and it produces neither a new C edge nor an MCP formula."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e032"],"rationale":"Submitted demand bids are also a price input to the double auction. This interface does not equate the originally declared quantities with the final dispatch quantities of Step 4."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"],"rationale":"Supply bids provide bid information for the MCP aggregate curve, whereas the quantities on the curve come from the final dispatch. The two local roles are kept distinct."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05"],"rationale":"The same paragraph simultaneously delimits the optional institutional forms of the MO and the responsibility to calculate prices from buyer and seller information. The choice of institution is not another pricing algorithm."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e003","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e032"],"rationale":"These citations correspond to the same frozen demand-bid functional node. The submitting parties, processing stages, and bid and dispatch roles of the chains still differ in scope, so all local citations are retained and the specific bid quantities are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e003","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e032"],"rationale":"The frozen nodes all denote the supply-bid function, but R006 also involves H-MG surplus-electricity suppliers, and R009 covers participant bids. The distinctions among chains are retained, and node identity is not used to equate suppliers or quantity scopes."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM003","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R009::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e032"],"rationale":"R009 explicitly uses the Nash-equilibrium dispatch result of the same Step 4, so the local clearing node of R003 is used as the display representative. Both original citations and the constraints are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM004","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R009::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-e003"],"rationale":"The two chains point to the same MO function of administering this market, receiving bids, and calculating prices. Only the node display is unified, and its optional institutional configuration is not removed."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM005","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e013"],"rationale":"The two items point to the same demand-side PBUC award and upper-bound rule, but the textual constraint and the expression that carries ordering symbols cannot be directly judged fully equivalent. In particular, the original wording of the demand ordering is ambiguous, so both expressions are retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B entries used by this cluster retain unverified status and have candidate-support eligibility only under the experimental policy. The B transcription, the C content, and this assembly have not received an independent source review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e003","v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e024","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031","v141-b-g02-e032"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Source correctness is to be judged only after manual checking of the original pages, formulas, and transcription. The present citation eligibility must not be interpreted as a passed audit."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"PBUC does not yet have an award-quantity variable, an allocation equation, or same-price handling. R006 writes the textual priority principle as an expression with ordering symbols and marks it as source, but the citation supplied has no corresponding original mathematical expression. The award wording in R003 cannot fill this gap in the formalization source.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e013"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether the original text provides allocation mathematics and handling of tied bids, and have subsequent C work clarify the formalization source of the ordering expression. This round keeps the frozen content."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G003","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The demand-side citation describes both ascending ordering and the highest demand price receiving the purchase award. R006 uses the latter to express priority. At this stage, the complete ordering direction or the award sequence cannot be confirmed on this basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e013"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original demand-side PBUC text and the related process description, and clarify the ordering direction and the meaning of being awarded. Before that clarification, retain the alternative expressions and do not claim that the contradiction has been resolved."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G004","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"It is not yet clear whether the H-MG bids used by R006 and the load-related bids in Eq. (5) are the PBUC surplus-electricity supply bids. The correspondence between the sign of the retailer price and the supply and demand bid categories also relies mainly on Eq. (12) and the context.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-hmg-offer-price","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-retailer-supply-offer-price","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-theta-retailer-demand-offer-price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e023"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the definition, stage of use, and buy or sell direction of each bid. Before confirmation, do not treat identical symbols as the same use across stages, and do not substitute them for the MCP."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G005","category":"math_incomplete","description":"There is not yet an explicit conversion or identity constraint between the Step 3 award upper bounds in R003 and the expected-value upper bounds in Eq. (20)–(22). Whether scenario buy and sell power is the PBUC scenario award quantity is not explicitly stated by the existing objects. The correspondence of time scale and units between award energy and power bounds is also not closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C008","v141-c-R003::x::var_p_retailer_sell_scenario_its","v141-c-R003::x::var_p_retailer_buy_scenario_its","v141-c-R003::theta::par_ev_retailer_sell_it","v141-c-R003::theta::par_ev_retailer_buy_it"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P4"],"required_work":"Additionally check the scenarios, units, indices, and expectation relationship of the PBUC outputs, and have C make the interface explicit. Until then, retain only the functional coupling and do not establish a same-quantity mapping."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G006","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R003 does not fully carry the NIRA response, the relaxation iterations, or the player objective functions. Eqs. (14)–(19) are covered mainly by procedural citations, and equipment limits, SOC state, and SOC evolution have also not been fully formed as independent constraint objects. Scenario generation and initial-schedule generation in Steps 1 and 2 are likewise not fully represented by the existing chains, so the complete dispatch solution cannot be reconstructed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::var_nira_x_i","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e015","v141-b-g02-e016","v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g02-e023","v141-b-g02-e025","v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g02-e028","v141-b-g02-e029"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"After the scope is made explicit, subsequent C is to add source-supported objective, algorithm, and physical-constraint objects and to state the external initial data. This round does not copy B formulas to fill the frozen catalog."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G007","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The retailer summation upper limit in Eq. (13) is retained as n, whereas the retailer index domain uses n'' separately. Eq. (20) retains the paired notation, and the interpretation of its two independent bounds still awaits source confirmation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C009","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e023","v141-b-g02-e024","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original formula images and the index definitions. If a typesetting or interpretation problem is confirmed, the revision is to be recorded by subsequent C. This round does not, on its own authority, correct the summation upper limit or split and rewrite the formulas."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The value 5 of ζ in R003 comes from the Table 5 simulation inputs, whereas the textual scope of the chain is general Step 4 dispatch. That case value cannot, without an accompanying statement, become a general upper-bound coefficient for all market instances.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::par_zeta_rld_nrl","v141-c-R003::x::var_p_rld_jt"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e029","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g04-E01"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manual review and subsequent C are to make explicit the case scope of applicability of this value, and the distinction between the general symbolic constraint and the instance value is to be retained. This round retains the existing parameters."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G009","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R009 provides only a procedural pricing rule for the intersection of the aggregate curves. It does not define an independent MCP symbol, curve objects, or the price selection when there is no intersection or when there are multiple intersections. Eq. (5) belongs to the H-MG bids and cannot be used to supply an MCP formula.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C003","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e032"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether explicit definitions of aggregation and of intersection selection exist. If they do not, continue to retain the procedural pricing candidate and do not fabricate a price equation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G010","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Retailer identity, HEMS, and explicit transaction upper bounds still involve proposals awaiting approval. The existing bid, MO, and clearing nodes do not mean that these objects have been approved, nor can retailers be equated with prosumers or HEMS be equated with the MO.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R006::V::matching.counterparties"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e013"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P1","v141-b-g02-prop01","proposal:v141-b-g03-retailer-participation","v141-b-g01-P2","v141-b-g01-P4"],"required_work":"Manually review the proposals and how they overlap, and then decide whether to extend the ontology and update the C bindings. D only cites proposal identifiers and does not insert new nodes."}]},"rule_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R001","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R002","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R004","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R006","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R003","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-5f20fde124935957","COMP-6436cfaf98af8d01","COMP-89ca1857e29bb0c7","COMP-db24d9fbcd9569b7","KG40-12aedc3eec573697","KG40-20f45ec4bdcbac06"]});
